+# LiteWing V2.6.C target contract
+
+This file is added by the `lrrk-air-mini` LiteWing adapter. It is a source
+contract for the first ESP32-S3 target implementation; it does not claim that
+the target is flashable or hardware validated.
+
+## Board identity
+
+- Board type: `0x13`
+- Board revision: `0x02`
+- MCU: ESP32-S3-WROOM-1
+- Recovery firmware: the existing upstream LiteWing ESP-Drone image
+
+## Required peripherals
+
+| Function | Pin or interface |
+| --- | --- |
+| MPU6050 SDA | I2C0 GPIO11 |
+| MPU6050 SCL | I2C0 GPIO10 |
+| MPU6050 data ready | GPIO12 |
+| Motor 1 | GPIO5 |
+| Motor 2 | GPIO6 |
+| Motor 3 | GPIO3 |
+| Motor 4 | GPIO4 |
+| Battery sense | ADC GPIO2 |
+| UART0/USB bridge | CH340K |
+
+The sensor path must probe the MPU6050 identity before publishing data. A
+missing or stale IMU is an arming-blocking fault.
+
+## Brushed output contract
+
+The board drives four brushed motors through low-side MOSFETs. Actuator values
+are clamped to `0..1000` and mapped to deterministic 20 kHz duty. Zero is the
+safe value. Initialization, disarm, failsafe, sensor fault, transport loss,
+and shutdown must write zero to all four channels. There is no ESC calibration
+or 1000-2000 microsecond servo-pulse path.
+
+Quad-X corner order is provisional until a human verifies the physical motor
+corners and IMU frame with props removed.
